From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:38:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 147/151] Find: fast Replace all for replacements that add or
 remove line breaks

cosmic-text moves every line behind an edit that adds or removes a line
break, so Replace all made one such move per match: minutes for 50,000
matches in a 5 MB file. When the moves would outweigh the lines spanned,
the lines from the first match to the last are now rewritten in one go
(deleted and inserted in pieces), keeping each line's own ending, as one
undo step. Few matches still go one by one. The cursor and the In
selection range end are computed as before.

Adds an ignored benchmark (find_timings) on a generated 5 MB file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

